---
// The cheese eaten with its maggots alive, and why that is the point.
---

<p>
	I'm not known to be squeamish about food and I will try a lot, but Casu Marzu gets a hard pass from me.
</p>
<p>
	It's sardinian pecorino ripened by maggots, which wouldn't be too bad if it weren't for the fact that the maggots are still alive in the finished cheese, and also you are eating them.
</p>
